        "original_id": "34e93a19-0e9b-5caf-aaac-9d35d1741a7e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fabian Cowdrey, Chris Cowdrey, Colin Cowdrey\n- Organizations: Kent County Cricket Club, England cricket team\n- Concepts: family cricket lineage, Test centuries, batting records\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Cowdrey made 22 Test centuries for England, and this remained an England record until 2013.\n- Colin Cowdrey was the first batsman to score centuries against the six other Test-playing countries of his era—Australia, South Africa, the West Indies, New Zealand, India, and Pakistan—both at home and away.\n- Fabian Cowdrey became the first third-generation player to play for Kent County Cricket Club, following his father Chris Cowdrey and his grandfather Colin Cowdrey.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5267a06c-2c83-5f35-b211-4d1b9761f2a5",
        "text": "Page: Fabian Cowdrey. Sentence: He made history by becoming the first third generation player to play for the county, following his father, Chris Cowdrey, and grandfather Colin Cowdrey.\nPage: Colin Cowdrey. Sentence: Cowdrey made 22 Test centuries (an England record until 2013) and was the first batsman to make centuries against the six other Test playing countries of his era; Australia, South Africa, the West Indies, New Zealand, India and Pakistan, making hundreds against them all both home and away.",
